277
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:31,420
Yeah.

278
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:35,000
Oh, hey, I got a guy who comes in real handy for that kind of thing.

279
00:17:35,280 --> 00:17:36,500
And we can work him hard.

280
00:17:37,100 --> 00:17:38,520
Not too hard, no.

281
00:17:39,940 --> 00:17:42,500
Some sweet lady must be talking about me.

282
00:17:42,940 --> 00:17:44,620
I guess things have gotten pretty quiet.

283
00:17:44,940 --> 00:17:46,760
We should probably go look for the captain.

284
00:17:46,980 --> 00:17:47,500
Sounds good.

285
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:48,320
Already?

286
00:17:48,760 --> 00:17:49,920
See you later, you know!

287
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:50,720
Yeah.

288
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:51,800
Bye, Asta.

289
00:17:52,460 --> 00:17:54,220
Don't eat stuff you find on the ground.

290
00:17:54,520 --> 00:17:55,540
Hey, that's not fair!

291
00:17:55,920 --> 00:17:57,420
It's been years since I've done that.

292
00:17:57,880 --> 00:18:01,040
I was wondering if there was a way I could get in touch with you sometime.

293
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:02,160
Hey!

294
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:04,780
Stay away from my yodo, you steamy raccoon!

295
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:05,900
Blow my eyes!

296
00:18:05,980 --> 00:18:08,860
Are you trying to blind me with your sparkles, you evil head fast?

297
00:18:10,300 --> 00:18:11,360
Okay, that's it!

298
00:18:11,380 --> 00:18:13,040
I'm going to fry you up for sure!

299
00:18:14,040 --> 00:18:15,200
How do you see me?

300
00:18:18,200 --> 00:18:20,240
Next time I'm going to have fry both of them!

301
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:20,800
Let's go.

302
00:18:20,800 --> 00:18:25,960
I can't believe I actually said that!

303
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:28,640
The worst squad picking a fight with the best one!

304
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:30,020
Have I gone totally crazy?

305
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:31,060
What's the matter?

306
00:18:31,180 --> 00:18:32,760
You got a headache or something?

307
00:18:33,140 --> 00:18:35,760
Oh, man!

308
00:18:35,900 --> 00:18:37,600
I can't wait to swing a sword again!

309
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:40,120
I can get a duck that you don't nearly long enough!

310
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:41,800
Stress-eating, Charmy!

311
00:18:41,800 --> 00:18:43,800
How can they eat right now?

312
00:18:44,140 --> 00:18:45,360
Didn't they hear what I said?

313
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:45,680
Whoa!

314
00:18:45,840 --> 00:18:49,840
There's nothing like a heaping helping of dessert for turning a frown upside down!

315
00:18:52,320 --> 00:18:53,820
Hey, not bad.

316
00:18:53,820 --> 00:19:03,020
Honestly, what a vulgar bunch they are.

317
00:19:03,380 --> 00:19:05,820
You should really choose your friends more carefully, you know.

318
00:19:09,280 --> 00:19:11,920
Aren't you embarrassed to be seen with people like that?

319
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:13,440
Why would I be?

320
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:16,320
I've never felt that way once.

321
00:19:16,740 --> 00:19:18,320
I'm very proud of Asta.

322
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:19,600
He's my rival.

323
00:19:21,280 --> 00:19:23,500
A simpleton like that's your rival!

324
00:19:23,780 --> 00:19:24,920
And for what, anyway?

325
00:19:25,500 --> 00:19:27,440
Are you two in some kind of competition?

326
00:19:27,900 --> 00:19:29,000
That's right, yes.

327
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:32,160
That was a little abrupt back there.

328
00:19:32,580 --> 00:19:33,980
Should you have said a better goodbye?

329
00:19:34,560 --> 00:19:37,220
I thought you and that handsome Golden Dawn fellow were old friends.

330
00:19:37,420 --> 00:19:37,760
It's fine!

331
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:40,340
I'll see him on another battlefield someday.

332
00:19:40,940 --> 00:19:45,400
After all, me and him, we're aiming to become the Wizard King!

333
00:19:46,260 --> 00:19:47,580
The Wizard King?

334
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:48,320
Ha!

335
00:19:48,500 --> 00:19:49,340
That's ridiculous!

336
00:19:49,740 --> 00:19:52,000
And you aren't even embarrassed to say it, are you?

337
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:54,420
But maybe commoners just don't feel shame,

338
00:19:54,520 --> 00:19:56,980
especially one who's been raised high above his station.

339
00:19:56,980 --> 00:20:01,280
The Great Yuno, a backwoods commoner chosen by the four-leaf grimoire.

340
00:20:01,520 --> 00:20:03,360
I don't know what your problem is, sir Smirky,

341
00:20:03,420 --> 00:20:05,280
